From 131a05a188ea145f18607972d57bc12914b8f8ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim <107831991+SyntaxError-PEBKAC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 19:17:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/22] ducksteps: telemetry prompts name Mozilla, not the
 maintainer

-vendor-short-name was set to SyntaxError-PEBKAC, but Firefox does not
use that token as a "who built it" credit. It names the party that
receives data and vets extensions, and ducksteps changes neither: the
build ships stock telemetry endpoints and stock extension policy.

The result was a browser telling users, on first run, that it
"automatically sends some data to SyntaxError-PEBKAC so that we can
improve your experience", with matching checkboxes for sending technical
and interaction data and a daily usage ping to a named individual. None
of that data ever went anywhere near the maintainer. It goes to Mozilla,
exactly as it does in stock Firefox.

Set to Mozilla, which also corrects the extension trust warnings ("sites
restricted by X") and the search-data opt-in.

The About dialog is the one place the maintainer is genuinely being
credited, so community-2 now writes SyntaxError-PEBKAC literally rather
than through the token, which would otherwise have rendered "designed by
Mozilla and built by Mozilla".
---
 browser/branding/ducksteps/locales/en-US/brand.ftl | 12 +++++++++++-
 browser/locales/en-US/browser/aboutDialog.ftl      |  6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/browser/branding/ducksteps/locales/en-US/brand.ftl b/browser/branding/ducksteps/locales/en-US/brand.ftl
index b91a5e2e73de..6daefd5da59e 100644
--- a/browser/branding/ducksteps/locales/en-US/brand.ftl
+++ b/browser/branding/ducksteps/locales/en-US/brand.ftl
@@ -23,5 +23,15 @@
 # This brand name can be used in messages where the product name needs to
 # remain unchanged across different versions (Nightly, Beta, etc.).
 -brand-product-name = ducksteps
--vendor-short-name = SyntaxError-PEBKAC
+# Mozilla, NOT SyntaxError-PEBKAC. This token is not a "who built it" credit: Firefox uses
+# it for the party that receives data and vets extensions, and ducksteps changes neither.
+# It fills in the data-collection preferences ("Send technical and interaction data to X",
+# "Send daily usage ping to X"), the startup data-reporting notice, the extension trust
+# warnings ("sites restricted by X") and the search-data opt-in. ducksteps ships stock
+# telemetry endpoints, so every one of those goes to Mozilla. Naming the maintainer here
+# told users their browsing data was being sent to a person, which was both untrue and
+# needlessly alarming.
+# The About dialog credits the maintainer with a literal string instead, because that one
+# genuinely is a "built by" credit.
+-vendor-short-name = Mozilla
 trademarkInfo = Firefox and the Firefox logos are trademarks of the Mozilla Foundation.
diff --git a/browser/locales/en-US/browser/aboutDialog.ftl b/browser/locales/en-US/browser/aboutDialog.ftl
index a944602b2d73..d2de4d50d246 100644
--- a/browser/locales/en-US/browser/aboutDialog.ftl
+++ b/browser/locales/en-US/browser/aboutDialog.ftl
@@ -78,7 +78,11 @@ aboutdialog-submit-feedback = Submit Feedback
 
 community-exp = <label data-l10n-name="community-exp-mozillaLink">{ -vendor-short-name }</label> is a <label data-l10n-name="community-exp-creditsLink">global community</label> working together to keep the Web open, public and accessible to all.
 
-community-2 = { -brand-short-name } is designed by <label data-l10n-name="community-mozillaLink">Mozilla</label> and built by <label data-l10n-name="community-vendorLink">{ -vendor-short-name }</label>, with a <label data-l10n-name="community-creditsLink">global community</label> working together to keep the Web open, public, and accessible to all.
+# "SyntaxError-PEBKAC" is written out rather than using { -vendor-short-name }, because
+# that token now correctly resolves to Mozilla: it is the party that receives telemetry and
+# vets extensions everywhere else in the UI. This line is the one place the maintainer is
+# genuinely being credited, so it says so directly.
+community-2 = { -brand-short-name } is designed by <label data-l10n-name="community-mozillaLink">Mozilla</label> and built by <label data-l10n-name="community-vendorLink">SyntaxError-PEBKAC</label>, with a <label data-l10n-name="community-creditsLink">global community</label> working together to keep the Web open, public, and accessible to all.
 
 helpus = Want to help? <label data-l10n-name="helpus-donateLink">Make a donation</label> or <label data-l10n-name="helpus-getInvolvedLink">get involved!</label>
 
